  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="653edf1f-f6f0-4b63-aece-287be038b569" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d6ecaf8b-a27d-47f2-950b-bf6cbc2c53a0" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="320">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the following to answer questions 1–5.</para>
      <blockquote>
        <para>Based on past musical productions, a theater predicts selling \(400-8p\) tickets when each ticket is sold at \(p\) dollars.</para>
      </blockquote>
      <para>Answer questions a–g to complete the middle column in the table to find out how many tickets the theater expects to sell and what revenues it expects to receive at the given ticket prices.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Ticket price (dollars)</entry>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Number of tickets sold</entry>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Revenue (dollars)</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(5\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>\(360\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>\(1800\)</para>
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(10\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>a. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(15\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>b. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(20\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>c. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(30\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>d. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(45\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>e. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(50\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>f. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <para>\(p\)</para>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>g. _____</para>
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <para>When the price is \($10\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold? </para>
        <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! There are 320 tickets sold when the price is $10 per ticket.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="217116ac-3762-41b7-adab-fb18faba6211" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="280">
