  <!--q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="07c98345-4d1e-48fb-a140-5262be95feb6" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="50">
    <problem>
      <para>For which ticket price, listed in the table, will the theater earn no revenue? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The revenue is zero when the ticket price is $50. </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0fb440fa-4233-44d8-a119-a040725ecaa2" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="10">
    <problem>
      <para>Calculate the lowest price of a ticket that the theater should sell the tickets for if it must earn at least \($3,200\) in revenue to break even (to not lose money) on the musical production. (The calculated value may not be listed in the table.) </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The lowest price the theater should charge to at least make $3,200 and break even is $10 per ticket.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para> Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="fa2f0344-3f29-441e-b9f9-d90c4cda33a2" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="40">
    <problem>
      <para>Calculate the highest price of a ticket that the theater should sell the tickets for if it must earn at least \($3,200\) in revenue to break even (to not lose money) on the musical production. (The calculated value may not be listed in the table.)</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The highest price the theater should charge to make at least $3,200 and break even is $40 per ticket. Although not shown in the table, we can calculate that when \(p\) is $40, the expected revenue is \(40(400-8(40))\) or \(40 \cdot 80\), which is $3,200.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7617ff65-c7d1-4155-a872-5ae056ca9c63" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="\((50,000-400p) \cdot p\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((50,000-400p) \\cdot p\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((50,000p-400) \\cdot p\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((50,000p-400p)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((49,600p) \\cdot p\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>A company sells running shoes. If the price of a pair of shoes in dollars is \(p\), the company estimates that it will sell \(50,000-400p\) pairs of shoes.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((50,000-400p) \cdot p\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3cf96af7-0f03-45ae-8e35-07252044c9c1" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;The school expects to sell 160 mugs if the price is $5 each.&quot;, &quot;The school will earn about $1,000 if it sells the mugs for $10 each.&quot;, &quot;The revenue will be more than $700 if the price is between $5 and $14.&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;At $2 per coffee mug, the revenue will be $196.&quot;, &quot;The school expects to sell 160 mugs if the price is $5 each.&quot;, &quot;The school will lose money if it sells the mugs for more than $10 each.&quot;, &quot;The school will earn about $1,000 if it sells the mugs for $10 each.&quot;, &quot;The revenue will be more than $700 if the price is between $5 and $14.&quot;, &quot;The expected revenue will increase if the price per mug is greater than $10.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the following to answer questions 7–9.</para>
      <blockquote>
        <para>The function \(f\) represents the revenue in dollars the school can expect to receive if it sells \(220-12x\) coffee mugs for \(x\) dollars each.</para>
        <para>Here is the graph of \(f\).</para>
        <image alt="Parabola on grid. Horizontal axis, price in dollars, from 0 to 20. Vertical axis, revenue in dollars, from 0 to 1000. Parabola opens down. Vertex near 9 comma 1000. \(\(x\)-intercepts near 0 and 18 point 2." height="209" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/705dd39386a32f3133aec603e335440f11bbffdb" width="324"/></blockquote>
      <para>Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> statements that describe this situation.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The school expects to sell 160 mugs if the price is $5 each. The school will earn about $1,000 if it sells the mugs for $10 each. The revenue will be more than $700 if the price is between $4 and $14.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5d533ed9-4520-4ef5-a252-6d5b25ea619c" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1000">
    <problem>
      <para>To the nearest hundred dollars, what is the maximum revenue for the mugs? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 1000</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.7.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f919514b-7f1b-4f68-9eb8-bc27744cab64" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="\(0 \leq x \leq 18\)" data-solution-options="[ &quot;\\(0 \\leq x \\leq 9\\)&quot;,&quot;\\(0 \\leq x \\leq 18\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0 \\leq x \\leq 1000\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x \\geq 0\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which is the approximate domain?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(0 \leq x \leq 18\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
